      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَايَثَةُ</span></b>  <i>He did, acted,</i> or <i>dealt, with him in
the manner of the lion:</i> or <i>he contended with him
for the glory of resembling the lion.</i> (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<i>He parted,</i> or <i>separated himself, from him;</i>
syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَايَلَهُ</span>. (TA.)

